  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated Community Development programme (ICDP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated Community Development Programme (ICDP) is an initiative of the Diocese of Marsabit resulting from consultative programme development processes that the Diocese engaged in during the last half of the year 2007. The programme focuses on justice and peace and sustainable livelihoods issues within the diocese. 

This is  a second cycle grant for  ICDP that is based on the recognition of the increasing intensity and frequency of drought and conflict in Northern Kenya. Reduced recovery periods between droughts and increased conflict that are breaking down existing coping strategies and increasing vulnerable households&#x2019; need to depend on external interventions.   Assessments conducted in affected areas in the last few months of 2010, revealed that pastoral communities have been particularly badly affected by repeated cycles of conflict and drought. The regular loss of livestock, inadequate recovery periods, poor governance, shortage of pasture and water have undermined traditional coping mechanisms and increased conflict over natural resources. Repeated humanitarian interventions have done little to strengthen affected communities&#x2019; capacity to cope with drought. An external evaluation was done for the ICDP in October 2010 with  recommendations  that  indentified gaps during the evaluation also formed the basis of this project.</narrative>
  </description>
